---
/**
 * The full help text (allowing the app to open, install, permissions, use,
 * update, remove, retained data). Headings carry ids so other pages can
 * deep-link to a section, such as Download's Open Anyway link.
 */
import StepList from "./StepList.astro";
import {
  installSteps,
  permissionsTroubleshooting,
  removeSteps,
  retainedData,
  settings,
  updateSteps,
} from "../content/site";
import { links } from "../lib/release";

const H = "h2";
---

<div class="prose help">
  <H id="open-anyway">App blocked by macOS?</H>
  <p>RecordStuff is not notarized by Apple, so macOS can block it the first time you open it and again after an update. Clicking Done only dismisses the warning; allow the app here instead.</p>
  <ol>
    <li>Manually open <strong>System Settings → Privacy &amp; Security</strong>.</li>
    <li>Scroll down to <strong>Security</strong> near the bottom.</li>
    <li>Find the RecordStuff message, click <strong>Open Anyway</strong> and confirm.</li>
  </ol>
  <p class="dim">Only allow a download you trust. Managed Macs may restrict this. For malware or damaged-file warnings, stop and report the issue. <a href={links.appleOpenAnyway} target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Apple’s instructions ↗</a></p>

  <H id="install">Install and first launch</H>
  <p>No Terminal, developer tools or certificates are needed. Files with <code>arm64</code> in the name are for Apple silicon Macs.</p>
  <StepList steps={installSteps} />
  <div class="callout">
    <p><strong>Two separate permissions.</strong> {permissionsTroubleshooting}</p>
  </div>

  <H id="use">Record</H>
  <p>Left-click the menu bar icon, or press <kbd>⌘</kbd><kbd>⇧</kbd><kbd>1</kbd> from any app, to record the selected screen and system audio. A stopwatch replaces the icon and a faint 3, 2, 1 counts down at the top-right of the recorded screen; the digits are gone before capture begins, and REC appears once it has. Click or press again during the countdown to cancel it (so does <em>Cancel recording</em> in the menu; nothing is saved), or while recording to stop. Choose Off, 5 or 10 seconds under <em>Recording settings → Countdown</em>; each digit also plays a soft tick, which never reaches the recording, and <em>Countdown sound</em> right below turns it off. Recordings are saved to Movies → RecordStuff by default; click the saved notification or choose <em>Show last recording</em> from the menu to find the file. Right-click and choose <em>Settings</em>, or press <kbd>⌘</kbd><kbd>⌥</kbd><kbd>,</kbd>. Under <em>Recording settings → Screen</em>, choose the primary display or a connected display. A specific display must be available; the app will not silently record another screen. The panel includes these settings, under Recording settings unless noted:</p>
  <div class="table-scroll" role="region" aria-label="Settings" tabindex="0">
    <table>
      <thead><tr><th>Setting</th><th>Options</th><th>Default</th></tr></thead>
      <tbody>
        {settings.map((row) => (<tr><td>{row.setting}</td><td>{row.options}</td><td>{row.fallback}</td></tr>))}
      </tbody>
    </table>
  </div>
  <p>Recording captures one whole screen, with no microphone, window or region selector. General settings also include System / Light / Dark appearance (System by default) and notifications (on by default, subject to macOS permission). Only language and appearance can change during recording.</p>
  <p>Output is H.264/AAC MP4. Audio requests 256 kbps with voice processing disabled. Actual bitrate depends on the encoder and content.</p>

  <H id="language">Language</H>
  <p>RecordStuff starts in English. Right-click the icon and choose <em>Settings → General → Language → <span lang="zh-Hant">繁體中文</span></em> for Traditional Chinese. The choice is saved and can change during a recording without affecting capture settings. Diagnostics stay English; macOS permission dialogs follow the system language.</p>

  <H id="update">Update manually</H>
  <p>Use Check for updates… in Settings → General to find a newer version and open its download page. Check for updates on launch is optional, on by default, and runs at most once per 24 hours. Checks wait while recording. Installation stays manual; older builds without update checks can use the download page directly.</p>
  <StepList steps={updateSteps} />

  <H id="remove">Remove</H>
  <StepList steps={removeSteps} />
  <p>Removing the app leaves your data in place. The app never deletes recordings. Delete these yourself only if you no longer need them:</p>
  <div class="table-scroll" role="region" aria-label="Retained data locations" tabindex="0">
    <table>
      <thead><tr><th>Data</th><th>Location</th></tr></thead>
      <tbody>
        {retainedData.map((row) => (<tr><td>{row.data}</td><td><code>{row.location}</code></td></tr>))}
      </tbody>
    </table>
  </div>
  <p>In Finder choose Go → Go to Folder and paste a path to open it. Any remaining entry under Privacy &amp; Security → Screen &amp; System Audio Recording can be removed there; this is optional.</p>
  <p class="dim">The same guide is on GitHub in <a href={links.installGuide} target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">English</a> and <a href={links.installGuideZh} hreflang="zh-Hant" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Traditional Chinese</a>, pinned to the released commit.</p>
</div>

<style>
  .table-scroll {
    overflow-x: auto;
    margin: 1rem 0 1.5rem;
  }
  .table-scroll table {
    margin: 0;
  }
  .help :global(.steps) {
    margin: 1rem 0 1.5rem;
  }
</style>
